# RZ/T2N u-boot
## Overview
This repository contains v2024.07 u-boot from https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/tree/v2024.07
along with Renesas RZ/T2N driver updates. 
For detailed notes on upstream u-boot please refer to https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/blob/v2024.07/README

## Build
The commands list to build the u-boot for RZ/T2N

`make clean`

`make rzt2n-dev_defconfig`

`make`

For preparing FIP image please refer to RZ/T2N TF-A manual

## SCIF Programming

Please refer to document "r01us0780ej0020-rzt2n(Linux_Start-up_Guide_RZT2N).pdf" with the following changes:

1. The FIP size **increased** from a1 release. Hence use the SCIF FIP programming command below:

   `XSPIW 0 0x060000 0xff000` 

2. The TF-A and u-boot connected to SCI0. Please note the Flash writer is using SCI1. Follow the procedure below:

   2a. Use SCI1 channel for Flash writer

   2b. Use SCI0 channel for TF-A, u-boot and Linux kernel


## Features / Limitations
1. The ethernet port enabled on this version of u-boot is ETH1. Connect the Ethernet cable on ETH1 J42
2. For ETH1 to work the SW7 requires the settings SW7-7: ON, SW7-8: OFF
3. For eMMC to work the SW7 requires the settings SW7-7: ON, SW7-8: ON

## TFTP / NFS
1. This requires the TFTP and NFS server to be setup correctly.
2. The kernel, device tree and root files to be accessible from the board ok for this remote booting to work.
Environment setting example ( Please change the path and IP address etc as per your environment)

`setenv serverip 192.168.10.3;` 

`setenv ipaddr 192.168.10.7;` 

`setenv bootfile Image;` 

`setenv fdtfile r9a07g076m43-dev.dtb;`  

`setenv nfsroot "/tftpboot/RZT2N/";`

`setenv rootpath "/tftpboot/RZT2N/";`

`setenv bootargs "ignore_loglevel root=/dev/nfs rw nfsroot=${serverip}:${rootpath},nfsvers=3 ip=${ipaddr}:${serverip}::255.255.255.0:t2n:eth0:off"`

`setenv bootcmd "tftpboot 0xc4200000 ${bootfile}; tftpboot 0xC5F00000 ${fdtfile}; run bootimage";`

